From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Schaefer <max@excloo.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 19:57:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 1059 redfin: probe native geometry without a default surface

CONTROLLED EXPERIMENT, not an established CoreAnimation contract or fix.
Only sweetfb_native=2 makes selector 3 return success with one output,
MACH_PORT_NULL. Both framebuffer and HID geometry already treat native as
nonzero, so mode 2 keeps mode 1's native dimensions without another boot
argument. Modes 0/1 retain the existing default-surface port path exactly.

The physical fSurface is still created and retained in every mode for the
console, CPU/GPU fallback and existing physical-display ownership. No other
selector or nil response changes. Keep the existing slot, three-frame,
fence, use-count and latch gates; rowkeep1, deadfill1, thermal, camera and
haptic behaviour are unchanged.

The native 1058 trial had a valid 1080x2340/BPR4352 scanout-slot surface, but
all 8 logged early rejects referred to the fixed physical default surface
with mask 1/slot 0. Aggregate windows showed 162 nonslot and 160 held frames,
with no direct entry or latch. Omitting that default might let CA allocate
a complete normal backboardd slot chain; successful-null fallback is NOT
proven by primary consumer source. The pinned public framebuffer below
instead returns NoMemory when it cannot provide a nonnull default:
https://github.com/Evsio0n/instantnoodle-xnu/blob/4b3afed623664548bfb09aa8c3eb0afd6dccb5d1/xnu/files/iokit/Kernel/MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp

Prepare a separate temporary native2 image with the matching native ADT.
Bound first startup/interaction, inspect actual slot geometry, direct
frames/latches and the physical panel, and return to verified
canvas-base1058 on blank output, a CA failure or failure of those gates.
No performance comparison is valid before rendering and direct scanout
work. The probe is authorised for controlled testing, not activation as a
normal preset. There is no speed or correctness result for this patch.

Also correct diagnostic p disp: .on without .geom is "armed", not
"direct". Snapshot under fLock and leave sweet_scan_live() and all its
internal scheduling/SwapWait/power consumers unchanged.

Provenance: current local patched 1058 source, local 1058 native geometry
experiment and its private aggregate trial evidence. No external code,
Apple material or firmware is imported; existing licences stay intact.

---
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -295,7 +295,7 @@
  * rdar://45025538 bar for 360x800 points). The display is therefore
  * presented as the iPhone X panel, 1125x2436 (375x812 points @3x), and the
  * centered 1080x2400 part of it is shown on the 1080x2400 panel.
- * Boot-arg sweetfb_native=1 presents the real panel size instead.
+ * Boot-arg sweetfb_native=1 presents the real panel size; =2 also probes a null default surface.
  */
 #define SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_W              1125
 #define SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_H              2436
@@ -330,6 +330,7 @@
 	uint64_t      fPhys;
 	uint32_t      fWidth, fHeight, fRowBytes;
 	uint32_t      fLogicalW, fLogicalH;     /* size reported to userland */
+	bool          fNullDefaultProbe;        /* 1059: sweetfb_native=2 only, unknown CA null-surface contract */
 	int32_t       fOffX, fOffY;             /* logical origin of the panel */
 	uint32_t      fCornerRadius;    /* panel pixels; boot-arg sweetfb_corner_radius */
 	uint32_t      fCornerExt;       /* rows/columns a corner covers */
@@ -984,6 +985,7 @@
 	}
 	int native = 0;
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetfb_native", &native, sizeof(native));
+	fNullDefaultProbe = native == 2;
 	fLogicalW = fWidth;
 	fLogicalH = fHeight;
 	if (!native && fWidth <= SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_W && fHeight <= SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_H) {
@@ -3906,7 +3908,11 @@
 {
 	if (end - s >= 4 && !strncmp(s, "disp", 4)) {
 		/* 0991: p disp: the display power state, for scripts (tools-claude/redfin-fpsbench.sh) */
-		IOLog("SWEET FB: display %s (p disp; scanout %s)\n", fPowerOff ? "off" : "on", sweet_scan_live() ? "direct" : "panel buffer");
+		IOLockLock(fLock);
+		bool off = fPowerOff;
+		const char *scanout = sweet_scan.geom ? "direct" : sweet_scan.on ? "armed" : "panel buffer";
+		IOLockUnlock(fLock);
+		IOLog("SWEET FB: display %s (p disp; scanout %s)\n", off ? "off" : "on", scanout);
 		return;
 	}
 	if (end - s >= 5 && !strncmp(s, "phase", 5)) {
@@ -4917,7 +4923,8 @@
 
 	switch (selector) {
 	case kSweetFBGetLayerDefaultSurface:
-		out[0] = sweet_surface_port_in_task(fFB->fSurface, fTask);
+		/* Controlled native2 probe: keep the physical surface for the console and fallback paths. */
+		out[0] = fFB->fNullDefaultProbe ? MACH_PORT_NULL : sweet_surface_port_in_task(fFB->fSurface, fTask);
 		outCount = 1;
 		break;
 	case kSweetFBSwapBegin:
